import{_ as t,o as a,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.C3idr2hZ.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Reusable agent packages","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"docs/agent-packages.md","filePath":"docs/agent-packages.md","lastUpdated":1793920704000}'),s={name:"docs/agent-packages.md"};function i(r,e,d,l,c,p){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="reusable-agent-packages" tabindex="-1">Reusable agent packages <a class="header-anchor" href="#reusable-agent-packages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reusable agent packages&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The dashboard&#39;s <strong>Packages</strong> page owns both OpenAPM (<code>apm.yml</code>) and portable <a href="https://agent-plugins.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Agent Plugins v1.0.0</a> (<code>plugin.json</code>). Agents remains the editor for shared specialist profiles.</p><p>Import a package folder, inspect its original files, then choose <strong>Use package</strong>. Select the coding agent, local or configured SSH host, working folder, and chat or terminal destination. An ORC project is optional: its folder can fill the path, which remains editable. <strong>Browse</strong> lists folders on the selected SSH host or opens the local folder picker. Saved agent definitions have the same <strong>Launch agent</strong> dialog. Terminal launches run preparation before starting the agent. Chat launches wait for preparation before opening a persistent conversation; use a terminal if an installer needs trust, authentication or conflict prompts. Chat supports Claude and Codex; Copilot uses the terminal destination.</p><p><strong>Export package</strong> downloads a ZIP preserving the original manifest and assets. The CLI&#39;s <code>orc agent-package import &lt;folder&gt;</code> and <code>orc agent-package export &lt;name&gt; &lt;new-folder&gt;</code> support both formats too. When a folder has both manifests, choose the desired format explicitly in the UI. The CLI uses OpenAPM when <code>apm.yml</code> is present.</p><h2 id="supported-deployment-routes" tabindex="-1">Supported deployment routes <a class="header-anchor" href="#supported-deployment-routes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supported deployment routes&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tooling</th><th>Packages</th><th>Agent</th><th>Requirements</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Microsoft APM</td><td>OpenAPM</td><td>Claude, Codex, Copilot</td><td>APM &gt;= 0.33.0 and the chosen agent CLI</td></tr><tr><td>Microsoft APM</td><td>Whole portable Agent Plugin, including native MCP configuration</td><td>Copilot</td><td>APM &gt;= 0.33.0, Copilot &gt;= 1.0.81, Git repository root</td></tr><tr><td>Native Codex plugin installer</td><td>Whole portable Agent Plugin, including skills, MCP and assets</td><td>Codex</td><td>Codex CLI &gt;= 0.162.1</td></tr><tr><td>Vercel skills</td><td>Skills-only portable Agent Plugin</td><td>Claude, Codex, Copilot</td><td>Bundled skills 1.7.2, Node.js &gt;= 22.20 and the chosen agent CLI</td></tr></tbody></table><p>APM and coding-agent executables must already be installed on the selected host. The <strong>Install for coding agent</strong> action applies package configuration; it does not install APM, Bun, or the coding-agent executable. Bun is required for preparation. On the API machine, <code>ORC_APM_PATH</code> can specify its executable. <code>ORC_COPILOT_PATH</code> selects a Copilot executable for package launches. Vercel skills ships with the npm distribution; standalone builds may use <code>skills</code> on PATH or <code>ORC_SKILLS_PATH</code>.</p><p>Deployment is persistent. For SSH, ORC transfers selected source files to a private staging folder under the working folder&#39;s <code>.orc/</code> directory before preparation. APM extends the working folder&#39;s <code>dependencies.apm</code> in <code>apm.yml</code>, retaining other configuration and existing dependencies; serialization may reformat YAML. ORC replaces earlier generated SSH source entries for the selected package on relaunch, preserving user-managed dependencies and other package selections. APM then owns dependency resolution, locking, target deployment and admission. Vercel copies selected skills into its normal project destinations. Existing project configuration and packages may also be available to the agent. ORC does not grant folder trust or add permission-bypass flags. Resolve upstream trust/authentication/conflict prompts in the terminal. Package code executes only through an explicit launch.</p><p>Codex uses its native marketplace and plugin commands for whole plugins. The source snapshot stays under <code>.orc/plugin-marketplaces/</code> in the working folder; each revision has a fresh content snapshot while its installed identity stays stable, so removed files do not remain active after reinstalling. The installed plugin and activation settings live in Codex&#39;s user cache/config on that host and can be available to other Codex sessions. Original catalog files are preserved. Copilot continues to use APM native registration. A skills-only deployment rejects packages containing root <code>mcp.json</code>. Shared specialist instructions and model selection support Claude and Codex; profiles with an explicit tool allowlist require Claude. Other combinations fail before launching instead of silently dropping those settings. On SSH, standalone agent instructions are applied but their referenced supporting files are not transferred; those paths must already be accessible on that host.</p><p>Imported plugin skills are discovered only at <code>skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</code> and use package-qualified identities in ORC. Invalid skills are isolated. Original resources and unknown metadata remain available for inspection/export. Agent Plugins supplies portable components, not a model or permissions profile; ORC&#39;s saved setup remains separate from its manifest.</p><p>The shared resolver lives in <code>@orc/core/package-launch</code>; the API&#39;s host preparation adapter serves terminal, chat and copied-command actions. Launch host selection does not change the installation&#39;s default SSH host. On Windows, where OpenSSH has no connection sharing, the API keeps one tunnel process per host and opens a connection per command.</p>',11)])])}const u=t(s,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,u as default};
